# Cloudflare Workers/Pages static-asset headers (mirrored into dist/ by
# Vite, since anything under public/ is copied to the build output root
# unchanged).
#
# Every JS/CSS file Vite builds has a content hash in its filename
# (index-XXXXXXXX.js), so it's safe — correct, even — to cache those
# forever: a new build always means a new filename, never the same URL
# with different content. index.html is the opposite: it's the only
# thing that references those hashed filenames, so if IT gets cached,
# the browser (or Cloudflare's edge) keeps loading an old build's JS/CSS
# indefinitely after a new deploy, which is exactly the "why doesn't my
# change show up" symptom this project kept hitting — a hard refresh
# always "fixed" it because that bypasses the browser cache, but nothing
# stopped it recurring on every future deploy without one. Forcing
# index.html to always revalidate closes that gap for good.

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
